1
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:07,270
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:12,700
Göktuğ!

3
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:14,200
Göktuğ!

4
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:20,330
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

5
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:21,540
Brother!

6
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:24,800
Osman!

7
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,600
Charge!

8
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:35,100
Alps!

9
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,200
Brothers!

10
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:38,740
My Bey.

11
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:42,780
-I will make all of them...
-May you hold on!

12
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:45,320
My Bey, pull it off.

13
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,940
Göktuğ, my brother, hold on!

14
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,560
Kill them all!

15
00:03:12,560 --> 00:03:14,940
May you hold on.

16
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:17,080
My brother.

17
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:28,500
I bear witness that there is no god but
Allah...

18
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:30,120
Göktuğ!

19
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:44,660
Göktuğ!

20
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,420
Göktuğ!

21
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:51,600
Göktuğ!

22
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:08,620
Göktuğ.

23
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:19,120
Alps!

24
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,820
Göktuğ is still alive. Take him away!

25
00:04:22,079 --> 00:04:24,180
Come on now!

26
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:25,820
My brother.

27
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:48,720
Savcı!

28
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,340
Do you even hear yourself, brother?

29
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:54,020
Nikola is a guest in this Tent.

30
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:04,200
Don't you remember what they did to us
while we were guests in Kulacahisar?

31
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:05,440
Savcı!

32
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:09,740
If we do the same thing, we'd be no
different from them!

33
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:15,980
We aren't that kind of profiteers who act
like friends while trying to stab others.

34
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:19,180
Are we, brother?

35
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:52,540
Dündar Bey, take Savcı and come with me.

36
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:57,260
Don't you know what kind of a trouble
is getting close to us?

37
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:00,660
Don't worry.

38
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:03,180
I will be there with him.

39
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:11,020
Gündüz Bey...

40
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:15,320
... after everything, you actually look
like a good person.

41
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,520
I'm sorry for what I did to you.

42
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,500
Or rather, for the things I did with
Flatyos.

43
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,580
Patience.

44
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:47,680
Gündüz Bey!

45
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:53,500
Enough already.

46
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:56,960
I also started to lose my patience,
Nikola.

47
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:02,560
Arslan Bey, wait a second.

48
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,900
Speaking of Flatyos...

49
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:08,620
... where is he?

50
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,980
He's no longer a commander of mine.

51
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:19,140
He is set out on his on now.

52
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:36,780
Where are you, Osman?

53
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,240
The battle has only just started brothers!

54
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:51,060
To the victory!

55
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,640
Charge!

56
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,320
Don't you ever retreat!

57
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,400
This is an order!

58
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:13,420
Charge!

59
00:08:36,419 --> 00:08:38,380
Do you understand me now, uncle?

60
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:46,260
I feel the same, my nephew.

61
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:50,240
I also want to take the head of that
Nikola dog.

62
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:54,340
However, we need to be patient.

63
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,940
We are here for a reason.

64
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:01,040
As long as we don't attract the anger of
Geyhatu, everything will be okay.

65
00:09:01,600 --> 00:09:03,340
Osman is not here, uncle.

66
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:05,200
What will we talk about?

67
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:08,920
Let Osman attract the anger of Geyhatun on
himself.

68
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:12,880
And together, we will take back
Kulacahisar.

69
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,300
We need to be patient.

70
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:20,480
I'm starting to lose my patience, uncle!

71
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:25,620
I have to look at Nikola's face while I
don't know what Osman is up to.

72
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:27,700
I have my own limits.

73
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:37,940
Real Arslan is not who is impatient but
who's capable of controlling his anger.

74
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:42,280
We need to be patient for Kayı.

75
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:45,020
We shall go back to Tent now.

76
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:48,180
As you say, uncle.

77
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:50,340
We will be patient for Kayı.

78
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:49,400
Oh, praise be upon my Valiant!

79
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:50,880
Where did you come from?

80
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:56,640
I came from Karabağ to help Kara Osman
defeat our enemies, my Bey.

81
00:10:57,700 --> 00:11:02,200
How wonderful! Praise be upon all
Valiants of Karabağ!

82
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,060
Come on now!

83
00:11:13,880 --> 00:11:14,820
Helen!

84
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:17,860
Bala!

85
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:20,400
Go after Helen!

86
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:38,560
I had done my duty and then I came here.

87
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:41,440
But Osman did not.

88
00:11:41,980 --> 00:11:43,880
He deceived us all.

89
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:51,520
It means he doesn't recognize might of
Geyhatu.

90
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:56,600
Thus, you need to talk Geyhatu about your
troubles on your own.

91
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:05,960
Don't worry Yalvak Arslan. I will tell
Geyhatu that you tried at least.

92
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:11,600
Tell Geyhatu that if he comes with his
army, I will also stand against him!

93
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:22,000
All Kayıs listen to my words but Osman
acts on his own.

94
00:12:22,420 --> 00:12:25,800
Geyhatu is free to attack Osman.

95
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:31,000
However, he can't touch even a single
hair of other Kayıs.

96
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:34,000
If he does, I will fight him too.

97
00:12:40,040 --> 00:12:41,720
I like courage.

98
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,780
You are too courageous, Yalvak Arslan.

99
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:51,360
Understand this well, Nikola.

100
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:57,240
Us Turks aren't so serious when our enemy
is as small as you but...

101
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:04,860
... we will combine all paths when the
enemy is as big as Mongols.

102
00:13:12,180 --> 00:13:16,220
Your paths combine with Cerkutay, Yalvak
Arslan.

103
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,380
What do you mean, Nikola?

104
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:25,560
Do you know where Cerkutay is, Yalvak
Arslan?

105
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:29,960
At the hands of Osman.

106
00:13:36,980 --> 00:13:37,820
That's right.

107
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:03,800
Ayaz!

108
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:05,040
Yes, my Bey!

109
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,640
Go to Yalvak's Tent at once!

110
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:11,160
Tell my uncle and brother not to try
hard for peace!

111
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,490
As you order, my Bey!

112
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:17,000
My Osman, it feels like we missed taking
castles after all.

113
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:19,980
Someday we will take Inegol and Bursa
too, my Bamsı Bey!

114
00:15:20,500 --> 00:15:21,320
Let's go!

115
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,740
Let's go, my child!

116
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,520
Targun Hatun!

117
00:16:28,540 --> 00:16:31,460
My father is caged down, Osman Bey. I just
couldn't wait!

118
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,180
Help him at once!

119
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:37,300
Alps!

120
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:40,140
Follow Targun Hatun!

121
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:26,680
Helen!

122
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:29,160
Helen!

123
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:33,500
Come at me! You unlucky Hatun.

124
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:37,100
Everything started when you and your
father came!

125
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,820
Die!

126
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:59,260
You will share the same end with Sofia!

127
00:19:07,540 --> 00:19:08,380
Bala!

128
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,780
Damn it!

129
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,340
Be quick!

130
00:21:05,420 --> 00:21:09,040
My Bey, the castle is finally with his
owner.

131
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:11,940
Oh, praise be!

132
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:16,280
Kulacahisar is a home to Turks from
now on!

133
00:21:26,300 --> 00:21:32,140
My Brothers! Rip out every flag you see
at the castle!

134
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:33,660
As your order, my Bey!

135
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:38,500
Let's go brothers.

136
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:04,160
Kara Osman is finally approaching.

137
00:22:14,140 --> 00:22:15,820
Damn it! Who is this dull stick?

138
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:39,420
Who are you?

139
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:41,560
Your death, Flatyos!

140
00:22:46,940 --> 00:22:48,960
Do you really want this, you dull stick?

141
00:22:51,260 --> 00:22:52,900
You are so brave, Flatyos.

142
00:22:54,300 --> 00:22:55,620
I like it.

143
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:39,020
-Targun Hatun.
-Osman Bey!

144
00:23:39,820 --> 00:23:41,840
He is not my father!

145
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:45,480
They took my father away!

146
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,960
Targun Hatun, don't worry.

147
00:23:58,540 --> 00:24:00,280
I'm going to bring your father.

148
00:24:09,940 --> 00:24:10,960
Bala!

149
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:24,040
As I said, I'm going to bring your father
to you!

150
00:24:33,240 --> 00:24:34,560
We couldn't capture Helen.

151
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,260
She ran away.

152
00:24:54,140 --> 00:24:54,980
Let's go.

153
00:25:37,980 --> 00:25:40,180
Aren't you a tough dull stick?

154
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:42,640
You are dead now.

155
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,820
It's nice of you to bear death with a
smile.

156
00:26:02,140 --> 00:26:05,380
Kulacahisar is not yours anymore.

157
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:12,420
I'm laughing as to this.

158
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:17,000
What are you saying?

159
00:26:28,560 --> 00:26:29,620
You hurt me!

160
00:26:31,100 --> 00:26:36,600
I bear witness that there is no god
but Allah...

161
00:26:37,040 --> 00:26:42,900
... and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the servant and Messenger of Allah.

162
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:25,980
- Brother.
- My Bey.

163
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:30,280
- Are you okay?
- We took the castle.

164
00:27:32,480 --> 00:27:36,440
So, I'm okay, my Bey.

165
00:27:39,120 --> 00:27:41,040
They seared my wounds.

166
00:27:41,680 --> 00:27:46,160
Mashallah, my brother!

167
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:53,280
Let's go.

168
00:27:54,800 --> 00:27:58,120
- Bamsı Bey.
- My Osman!

169
00:28:01,120 --> 00:28:03,200
Mashallah, my valiant!

170
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:11,600
What's up with you?

171
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:15,360
Nothing. I'm fine.

172
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:55,560
Son of Ertuğrul Gazi, Osman Bey!

173
00:30:00,800 --> 00:30:05,520
Don’t kneel!
Keep standing!

174
00:30:05,520 --> 00:30:10,400
Stand like the mountains
against the evil!

175
00:30:13,600 --> 00:30:19,160
As your Alps, we're with you
until we die!

176
00:30:25,280 --> 00:30:27,800
As long as you progress
in the path of battle…

177
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:31,000
… clearing those roads is
our sacred duty!

178
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:55,000
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

179
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,880
Looks like Osman isn’t coming.

180
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:11,240
Everyone completed their duties.

181
00:31:13,480 --> 00:31:16,840
It’s time to dismiss this meeting.

182
00:31:21,640 --> 00:31:25,240
Next time, I’ll be waiting
for you at Kulacahisar.

183
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:28,800
We can also continue
with where we left off.

184
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:31,560
Uncle. You should come too!

185
00:31:32,880 --> 00:31:35,000
Uncle-nephew statue.

186
00:31:38,160 --> 00:31:39,960
Now I will--

187
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:44,320
Nikola!

188
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:51,480
I’ll kill you!

189
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:53,920
Soldiers, don’t interrupt!

190
00:31:54,200 --> 00:31:58,640
- Step aside!
- I will kill you!

191
00:31:58,640 --> 00:32:04,600
- Savcı!
- Savcı Bey!

192
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:08,080
- Savcı Bey!
- Stop!

193
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:13,640
As soon as we get out of this
mess, I’ll do the same to them!

194
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:17,080
Let me go!

195
00:32:20,320 --> 00:32:23,040
Ensheathe the swords!

196
00:32:28,120 --> 00:32:31,080
Savcı! Stop!

197
00:32:31,080 --> 00:32:33,600
You’re barbaric.

198
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:38,040
My Bey!

199
00:32:38,520 --> 00:32:40,440
What is it, Sertaç?

200
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:43,560
My Bey, a Greek is here.
He escaped from Kulacahisar.

201
00:32:43,560 --> 00:32:45,760
- So?
- Osman Bey!

202
00:32:45,840 --> 00:32:47,840
What happened to Osman Bey?

203
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:51,760
Osman Bey conquered Kulacahisar!

204
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:19,400
- Long live, Osman Bey!
- Long live, Osman Bey!

205
00:33:20,040 --> 00:33:26,480
My Alps! My brothers!
My valiants!

206
00:33:34,160 --> 00:33:39,360
This is not an honour,
a victory day.

207
00:33:40,800 --> 00:33:50,600
This is the day we
tear apart the acts of evil!

208
00:33:55,560 --> 00:34:03,880
Our greatest shame comes from not the
enemies who took this castle with tricks…

209
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:10,760
… but from those who are
from our own kind, own blood!

210
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:16,639
They took advantage of
Ertuğrul Gazi’s illness and…

211
00:34:16,639 --> 00:34:25,040
… worked together with the
enemies both outside and among us!

212
00:34:26,120 --> 00:34:34,080
From now on, our children
won’t feel this kind of shame!

213
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:36,880
We won’t allow it!

214
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:49,400
From now on, we tear
apart the chains on our feet!

215
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:56,800
Our next target is İnegöl Fortress!

216
00:34:59,080 --> 00:35:05,040
We shall not stop until
we capture the infidels’ castle!

217
00:35:05,040 --> 00:35:11,960
- We shall not stop!
- We shall not stop!

218
00:35:12,320 --> 00:35:16,760
Let those who are
from our own blood…

219
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:19,120
… get tricked by the enemy!

220
00:35:20,240 --> 00:35:27,040
Now, those who sharpen their
swords with faith will be victorious!

221
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:35,840
- Allahu akbar!
- Allahu akbar!

222
00:35:48,400 --> 00:35:52,520
Osman brought the end
of all of you with this victory!

223
00:35:52,760 --> 00:35:57,040
You’ll be crushed by
the Greek and Mongol armies!

224
00:35:57,040 --> 00:36:02,840
Beys! I lost a castle,
you lost everything you have left!

225
00:36:03,760 --> 00:36:06,400
Checkmate!

226
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:20,120
Dündar Bey, Gündüz Bey. Come.

227
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:24,920
No one goes to Kulacahisar.

228
00:36:26,920 --> 00:36:29,800
No one helps Osman.

229
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:35,600
Save yourselves first.

230
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:39,680
We should return to the Tent, uncle.

231
00:36:40,240 --> 00:36:43,560
And put an end
to these useless negotiations.

232
00:36:43,960 --> 00:36:48,200
Osman did his move.
Not it’s my turn.

233
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:50,760
Don’t make moves out of anger.

234
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:56,640
The enemy’s castle is conquered.
And the conqueror is our brother.

235
00:36:58,440 --> 00:37:02,760
Your brother risked the whole
Tent’s future by conquering that castle.

236
00:37:02,760 --> 00:37:06,480
We need precautions, Gündüz!

237
00:37:06,480 --> 00:37:10,520
Geyhatu will come
again and shed blood!

238
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,960
What are you talking about, uncle?

239
00:37:12,960 --> 00:37:15,760
We should let him kill Osman
and be done with it?

240
00:37:18,560 --> 00:37:20,120
What about you, Savcı?

241
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,720
Is that what we should do?

242
00:37:45,920 --> 00:37:54,000
Brother. If you’re not doing
well, you should stay here with Bamsı Bey.

243
00:37:54,920 --> 00:38:00,600
I’m okay, my Bey. Don’t worry.
Once I’m on my horse, the rest is easy.

244
00:38:03,040 --> 00:38:07,120
Very well.

245
00:38:10,680 --> 00:38:12,560
Let’s go, brother.

246
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:26,400
Bamsı Bey!
The castle is yours now.

247
00:38:29,040 --> 00:38:35,520
Don’t worry, son! While we’re
here, no one will dare come here!

248
00:38:35,520 --> 00:38:38,360
If they do, they’ll meet their maker.

249
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:42,480
Watch out for yourself.

250
00:38:42,880 --> 00:38:49,640
When the day comes,
we’ll establish our state side by side!

251
00:38:52,720 --> 00:38:57,160
Inshallah, my Osman.
Don’t worry!

252
00:38:57,160 --> 00:39:01,160
Bamsı is here as long
as Allah lets him!

253
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:05,160
- Thank you!
- My valiant!

254
00:39:06,320 --> 00:39:07,520
Here.

255
00:39:11,120 --> 00:39:15,600
If you allow me, I’d like
to come with you, my Bey.

256
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:22,040
You’re very welcome, Gence Bey. Come.

257
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:36,600
We’re done with this castle.
Let’s go to our Tent.

258
00:40:47,960 --> 00:40:52,680
Peace is impossible now.
They are all over each other.

259
00:40:53,520 --> 00:40:55,760
We should save ourselves.

260
00:40:55,760 --> 00:40:59,520
Osman must not take
Cerkutay to Geyhatu.

261
00:41:00,160 --> 00:41:05,120
Let’s set off at once.
I’ll end Osman myself.

262
00:41:13,720 --> 00:41:18,160
Osman and Bala are nowhere
to be seen. Aygül also left.

263
00:41:18,880 --> 00:41:21,760
Targun Hatun also left running.

264
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:25,200
They’re up to something.

265
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:28,320
Osman must have gone to Kulacahisar again.

266
00:41:28,320 --> 00:41:30,800
He’s obsessed about that castle.

267
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:36,400
Bamsı Bey and his
Alps aren’t here either.

268
00:41:36,880 --> 00:41:41,920
If you’re right, and he takes the castle…

269
00:41:43,680 --> 00:41:46,880
If Ertuğrul Bey wakes up
and hears about it…

270
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:51,360
Then Osman will be
the successor and everything will be over.

271
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:57,280
Once Dündar and Savcı Bey are
here, we’ll see what their intentions are.

272
00:41:59,920 --> 00:42:05,800
If they still don’t want to
make a move to defeat Osman…

273
00:42:05,800 --> 00:42:10,880
… we’ll tell them that
there is no time left.

274
00:42:19,280 --> 00:42:23,200
If Osman Bey is trying
to take Kulacahisar, a war will break out.

275
00:42:23,200 --> 00:42:24,520
We’re in a war already.

276
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:27,960
I’m talking about the war
in Kayı Tent, Davud brother.

277
00:42:27,960 --> 00:42:29,440
They are brothers.

278
00:42:29,440 --> 00:42:33,760
Sure they are.
The worst kind of war.

279
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:36,480
You don’t know who
your enemy and friends are.

280
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:40,120
Look at me! You’re
trying to do your own thing again!

281
00:42:40,120 --> 00:42:42,200
Of course, you’re
relaxed, Davud brother.

282
00:42:42,200 --> 00:42:45,800
Once a war breaks out,
no one will care about a potter!

283
00:42:45,800 --> 00:42:48,920
Everyone will be
interested in your swords.

284
00:42:49,560 --> 00:42:51,640
You’re exaggerating again.

285
00:42:51,640 --> 00:42:56,120
My only intention is to trade,
brother. I’m trying to make ends meet.

286
00:42:56,120 --> 00:43:00,080
But unfortunately, no one
will make ends meet in Kayı Tent.

287
00:43:00,080 --> 00:45:21,760
[Call to Prayer]

288
00:45:24,640 --> 00:45:27,480
My Bey! Is there any good news?

289
00:45:27,480 --> 00:45:30,360
There is, Master Davud!

290
00:45:31,200 --> 00:45:33,080
Welcome, Osman Bey!

291
00:45:33,080 --> 00:45:35,080
Thank you, Ahmet Alp!

292
00:45:36,280 --> 00:45:43,680
Gence Bey! This is our
Ahmet Alp. He protects the Tent.

293
00:45:43,680 --> 00:45:45,240
I’m Gence Bey.

294
00:45:50,320 --> 00:45:54,080
My Bey! This arrival
looks like a blessed one!

295
00:45:55,640 --> 00:46:00,160
With the permission of Allah,
and veterans’ efforts…

296
00:46:00,160 --> 00:46:02,720
Kulacahisar is conquered once again.

297
00:46:02,720 --> 00:46:05,360
Mashallah!

298
00:46:06,240 --> 00:46:10,280
Kulacahisar is conquered!

299
00:46:10,280 --> 00:46:17,680
- Allahu akbar!
- Allahu akbar!

300
00:46:23,280 --> 00:46:26,240
Kulacahisar is conquered.

301
00:46:26,240 --> 00:46:29,440
Everything will be more difficult now.

302
00:46:34,800 --> 00:46:41,800
Master Davud, our guest is
tired from battle. Take care of him.

303
00:46:41,800 --> 00:46:44,400
With all my heart, my Bey!

304
00:46:49,640 --> 00:46:52,560
I’m honoured, my valiant.

305
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:53,960
I’m also honoured.

306
00:47:43,480 --> 00:47:51,360
Before we conquered it,
this Kulacahisar Castle...

307
00:47:51,360 --> 00:47:56,720
... was all about soulless rocks,
empty rooms.

308
00:47:57,120 --> 00:48:07,040
After it was washed with martyrs' blood
and blessed by the names of our creator...

309
00:48:07,960 --> 00:48:13,800
... then it became home,
and faith.

310
00:48:17,720 --> 00:48:25,200
Children! The enemy will come!
They will test your faith!

311
00:48:26,160 --> 00:48:32,520
They'll try to take your homeland!
they'll try to rape your honour!

312
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:35,200
What will you do then?

313
00:48:35,200 --> 00:48:37,480
We'll fight!

314
00:48:39,440 --> 00:48:42,600
- Will you give them this castle?
- Never!

315
00:48:42,600 --> 00:48:45,880
- Will you give them your flag?
- Never!

316
00:48:47,040 --> 00:48:52,280
"I'd rather die" you say. Is that correct?

317
00:48:52,480 --> 00:49:00,320
- It is not!
It is not!

318
00:49:02,040 --> 00:49:08,920
Dead or alive, this castle
will not be lost again!

319
00:49:10,240 --> 00:49:19,120
Doesn't matter if they're Greek or Mongol.
We'll crush them all!

320
00:49:19,120 --> 00:49:21,520
But they will not take this castle!

321
00:49:22,360 --> 00:49:29,960
Children! They will not say Bamsı and
his Alps died defending the castle!

322
00:49:30,520 --> 00:49:35,480
"Bamsı and his Alps didn't surrender
the castle" they will say!

323
00:49:35,480 --> 00:49:40,600
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

324
00:49:44,160 --> 00:49:54,920
Children! Kayı is becoming a beylic!
It's dreaming of becoming a state!

325
00:49:55,320 --> 00:50:05,160
Children! Don't burry this
dream with yourself! Live that dream!

326
00:50:06,880 --> 00:50:15,040
Children! Be an old veteran like
Bamsı Beyrek!

327
00:50:16,160 --> 00:50:20,360
Be glorious, be victorious!

328
00:50:21,200 --> 00:50:32,200
Children! Until the enemy surrenders,
until the people of Kayı sleep in peace...

329
00:50:32,480 --> 00:50:37,040
You don't get the sweet
release of death!

330
00:50:37,040 --> 00:50:43,480
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

331
00:50:47,600 --> 00:50:53,960
My Osman. My dark-eyed Osman
who conquered Kulacahisar again!

332
00:51:06,040 --> 00:51:13,160
Osman. The fact that you conquered
the castle again makes your aunt proud.

333
00:51:13,160 --> 00:51:20,320
But remember. Other things you want to do
for the second time doesn't make me happy.

334
00:51:33,600 --> 00:51:40,400
Aunt. You're their elders.
Give them advice.

335
00:51:47,280 --> 00:51:50,520
You did it again, Osman.

336
00:51:53,080 --> 00:51:55,720
You threw the Tent into the fire.

337
00:51:56,520 --> 00:52:06,400
You don't care about the situation your
uncle, your brothers are in, do you?

338
00:52:08,040 --> 00:52:10,520
Do you, Osman Bey?

339
00:52:29,760 --> 00:52:31,280
My Bey!

340
00:52:34,080 --> 00:52:36,040
Osman Bey is here.

341
00:52:37,720 --> 00:52:42,560
The people and Alps
are celebrating, my Bey!

342
00:52:43,840 --> 00:52:48,120
My Osman will be here any second.

343
00:52:49,000 --> 00:52:56,720
He'll stand by the door. When he
sees that his father's eyes are open...

344
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:04,160
Father!

345
00:53:07,360 --> 00:53:09,760
- Father!
- Son!

346
00:53:10,960 --> 00:53:12,600
Father!

347
00:53:16,680 --> 00:53:18,800
Are you okay?

348
00:53:36,120 --> 00:53:40,040
My veteran father!
My brave father!

349
00:53:41,480 --> 00:53:44,000
I see that you're doing well.

350
00:53:46,960 --> 00:53:48,800
You'e doing well.

351
00:53:51,480 --> 00:53:56,600
Where were you, my Osman?
What news did you bring?

352
00:53:56,600 --> 00:53:59,640
I kept my promise, father.

353
00:54:00,982 --> 00:54:03,502
Kulucahisar is again yours.

354
00:54:06,654 --> 00:54:11,524
It is in your land.

355
00:54:14,440 --> 00:54:18,760
My Allah, thank you.

356
00:54:28,566 --> 00:54:31,196
Thank you so much.

357
00:54:40,056 --> 00:54:44,626
I saw you, my son.
I saw you.

358
00:54:45,444 --> 00:54:48,084
I saw our lands.

359
00:54:48,868 --> 00:54:51,548
I saw the horizon.

360
00:54:53,643 --> 00:54:56,443
I saw the future.

361
00:55:03,132 --> 00:55:06,452
Tell me about the future, Osman.

362
00:55:10,023 --> 00:55:13,043
Tell me about the future.

363
00:55:22,990 --> 00:55:26,460
The war is coming, my father.

364
00:55:28,095 --> 00:55:33,069
This war will continue until we destroy
the ones...

365
00:55:33,069 --> 00:55:37,049
who want to end Kayıs forever.

366
00:55:38,367 --> 00:55:43,157
I am not going to stop until I kill them.

367
00:55:47,679 --> 00:55:51,719
After that, my people will relieve.

368
00:55:53,810 --> 00:55:57,870
Mosques, madrasahs...

369
00:55:58,523 --> 00:56:01,183
I will build arsenals.

370
00:56:02,624 --> 00:56:10,334
I will build so that our state takes root
in this land.

371
00:56:14,046 --> 00:56:19,426
So that our knowledge grows with our
faith.

372
00:56:19,461 --> 00:56:26,101
So that our sons and daughters spread
it through the world.

373
00:56:33,225 --> 00:56:34,555
Then...

374
00:56:39,476 --> 00:56:42,786
I give my blessings to you.

375
00:56:54,259 --> 00:56:56,249
My father.

376
00:57:02,604 --> 00:57:04,964
Alhamdulillah.
(praise be to Allah)

377
00:57:08,943 --> 00:57:11,433
My father.

378
00:57:19,941 --> 00:57:23,771
My one and only father.

379
00:57:37,203 --> 00:57:41,163
Osman is acting like a Bey.

380
00:57:41,601 --> 00:57:44,731
I hope it ends well.

381
00:57:48,451 --> 00:57:52,691
They say some were born to be Bey...

382
00:57:52,748 --> 00:57:56,578
and some always try to act like a Bey.

383
00:58:17,155 --> 00:58:20,945
It's high time we had a talk, Targun.

384
00:59:13,417 --> 00:59:18,547
How does it feel to lose a castle
two times, Helen?

385
00:59:25,524 --> 00:59:29,134
Feels like being captured two times
by the same man.

386
00:59:53,075 --> 00:59:57,605
Vladius and Helen.
Two great soldiers!

387
00:59:59,520 --> 01:00:04,340
We lost Kulucahisar.
Don't you think it was so fast, Helen?

388
01:00:04,713 --> 01:00:08,359
Osman's men infiltrated into us.
They opened the gates!

389
01:00:08,359 --> 01:00:11,919
And the Kulucahisar fell, right?

390
01:00:13,327 --> 01:00:18,197
And you run like a rat instead
of fighting like a soldier, right?

391
01:00:26,011 --> 01:00:27,821
And Vladius.

392
01:00:29,504 --> 01:00:32,844
You were supposed to kill Osman,
weren't you Vladius?

393
01:00:35,389 --> 01:00:40,009
While sitting in Yavlak Arslan's dirty
tent, everybody was waiting for Osman...

394
01:00:40,049 --> 01:00:44,819
I was thinking that "oh you can wait
for hours, but Osman is dead."

395
01:00:44,861 --> 01:00:49,841
But meanwhile, he conquered
Kulucahisar.

396
01:00:53,890 --> 01:00:56,240
Osman didn't come, Nicola.

397
01:00:56,627 --> 01:01:00,060
A yahoo showed up instead of him.
I killed him.

398
01:01:00,060 --> 01:01:03,810
A yahoo?
A yahoo.

399
01:01:03,863 --> 01:01:10,965
I didn't want you to kill a yahoo, Vladius.
I wanted you to kill the lion.

400
01:01:10,965 --> 01:01:16,280
If you listened to me and killed Osman
when we had the chance...

401
01:01:16,280 --> 01:01:21,816
now I wouldn't be hearing these insults,
and you wouldn't lose Kulucahisar.

402
01:01:21,816 --> 01:01:26,101
I send you to Sogut to fix
your fault, Vladius. But you failed.

403
01:01:26,101 --> 01:01:30,223
Moreover, Osman captured Cerkutay
because of your foolishness!

404
01:01:30,223 --> 01:01:34,943
Can you imagine what will happen if
he takes Cerkutay to Geyhatu?

405
01:01:39,801 --> 01:01:42,041
I will kill him.

406
01:01:44,641 --> 01:01:46,871
I'll kill Osman.

407
01:01:48,218 --> 01:01:51,798
I would be very happy, Vladius.

408
01:01:52,349 --> 01:01:55,639
But I am down for even Cerkutay.

409
01:01:58,423 --> 01:02:01,813
I'll take you Helen.

410
01:02:01,884 --> 01:02:07,434
As you know, we can't go to Kulucahisar.
Right?

411
01:02:11,890 --> 01:02:17,840
Can you at least find Osman, Vladius?

412
01:02:31,595 --> 01:02:34,945
We need to foresee every move
of Nicola.

413
01:02:35,159 --> 01:02:38,329
He won't simply attack the castle.

414
01:02:39,039 --> 01:02:41,609
He will make an unexpected move.

415
01:02:42,173 --> 01:02:47,163
As to Yavlakarslan, he must have heard
that we have Cerkutay.

416
01:02:47,578 --> 01:02:50,908
He is going to come like a fly goes
around the dirt.

417
01:02:51,895 --> 01:02:56,855
He is going to come here himself.

418
01:02:57,207 --> 01:03:00,107
Then I'll kill him.

419
01:03:00,622 --> 01:03:04,792
My Bey, he can't dare to come to
our tribe.

420
01:03:05,216 --> 01:03:11,086
He is not going to come to our tribe,
Göktuğ. He'll cross our path.

421
01:03:11,956 --> 01:03:18,326
Be ready. I will destroy whoever
disobeys Kayıs.

422
01:03:48,893 --> 01:03:51,713
First of all, I want it to be good.

423
01:03:54,185 --> 01:03:58,365
It is actual that Beys marry more than
one Hatun.

424
01:04:00,350 --> 01:04:07,460
Our Osman Bey made this decision to
keep the family name alive.

425
01:04:17,222 --> 01:04:21,302
What I am supposed to do as
Osman Bey's first Hatun is...

426
01:04:22,574 --> 01:04:25,554
to tell you about him.

427
01:04:28,860 --> 01:04:35,850
To prevent any flaws that can happen
to this man who is the hope for Kayıs.

428
01:04:37,456 --> 01:04:40,946
What a noble way of thinking.

429
01:04:41,455 --> 01:04:43,955
I am willing to listen to you.

430
01:04:50,953 --> 01:04:55,773
He doesn't like talking about wars and
favours he made.

431
01:04:58,916 --> 01:05:01,466
He is thoughtful in his tent.

432
01:05:03,577 --> 01:05:06,417
He thinks of the future of Kayı.

433
01:05:09,362 --> 01:05:12,532
You need to be silent those times.

434
01:05:15,648 --> 01:05:18,258
Then he says "my Bala."

435
01:05:24,794 --> 01:05:27,044
I mean...

436
01:05:27,117 --> 01:05:30,347
He's going to call you Targun,
of course.

437
01:05:38,176 --> 01:05:42,386
"How was your day, tell me."
he says.

438
01:05:44,275 --> 01:05:47,925
He listens to you with a clean smile
on his face.

439
01:05:51,038 --> 01:05:53,888
He listens, then he passes out again.

440
01:05:57,574 --> 01:06:01,994
Don't be offended.
My Sheik father was also like that.

441
01:06:02,826 --> 01:06:05,916
Big man are thoughtful.

442
01:06:07,732 --> 01:06:12,282
Bala Hatun, this must be hard for you.

443
01:06:12,282 --> 01:06:15,612
- Don't contunie.
- I have to say this.

444
01:06:18,500 --> 01:06:23,200
Our Osman Bey...
Osman...

445
01:06:28,929 --> 01:06:32,419
likes his beard warm.

446
01:06:33,555 --> 01:06:38,505
Cook it fast, or just heat it.

447
01:06:40,135 --> 01:06:43,155
- In the afternoon.
- Bala Hatun.

448
01:06:43,711 --> 01:06:47,451
- In the afternoon...
- Don't torture yourself.

449
01:06:54,602 --> 01:06:56,882
Osman Bey and I...

450
01:07:01,630 --> 01:07:04,384
We are actually...

451
01:07:04,384 --> 01:07:06,514
You, Targun Hatun.

452
01:07:09,432 --> 01:07:12,312
You are going to give him sons and
daughters.

453
01:07:13,992 --> 01:07:17,452
This is why I am okay with this marriage.

454
01:07:24,801 --> 01:07:28,291
I know, I know.

455
01:08:41,105 --> 01:08:44,685
Thank Lord.
We took the castle back.

456
01:08:53,131 --> 01:08:56,051
My horse is waiting for the race.

457
01:08:59,382 --> 01:09:02,532
You didn't forget, right?

458
01:09:02,711 --> 01:09:05,591
I remember.

459
01:09:08,919 --> 01:09:10,789
Are you not willing to do it?

460
01:09:16,662 --> 01:09:20,262
Gonca Hatun, why are you staring?

461
01:09:21,048 --> 01:09:27,248
Men like racing, right?

462
01:09:27,666 --> 01:09:32,896
We do, but what's the point?

463
01:09:34,791 --> 01:09:39,691
Osman Bey compares Bala to others.

464
01:09:42,557 --> 01:09:45,637
- My Bey does the right thing.
- Is that so?

465
01:09:49,524 --> 01:09:51,774
Gonca Hatun.

466
01:09:52,308 --> 01:09:54,628
We are going to race, right?

467
01:09:55,166 --> 01:09:58,286
Race yourself.

468
01:09:59,001 --> 01:10:00,371
Gonca Hatun!

469
01:10:09,487 --> 01:10:13,717
From now on, our job is diffucult,
my Bala.

470
01:10:13,867 --> 01:10:18,217
But, you will have hard days ahead of you.

471
01:10:19,500 --> 01:10:24,370
Don't ever let them to break your heart.

472
01:10:24,987 --> 01:10:30,687
You shall be strong.
Don't buckle under anyone!

473
01:10:31,815 --> 01:10:35,035
Now they are going to try to attack
you over Targun Hatun.

474
01:10:35,147 --> 01:10:40,007
Defend both yourself and Targun Hatun.

475
01:10:42,497 --> 01:10:48,827
You told me to follow her. You suspected
her, now you want me to defend her.

476
01:10:48,900 --> 01:10:52,780
Yes, my Bala.
That's what I want for now.

477
01:10:53,397 --> 01:10:58,277
You wanted me to marry.
I accepted.

478
01:10:59,293 --> 01:11:04,783
Now I want you to defend the Hatun
I will marry. Please accept this.

479
01:11:06,105 --> 01:11:10,245
Why did you choose her?
Not someone else but her?

480
01:11:12,106 --> 01:11:17,156
My Bala, I told you to follow her.

481
01:11:17,390 --> 01:11:22,580
I told you that I suspected her.
I was right.

482
01:11:24,175 --> 01:11:28,973
Targun Hatun works for Nicola.

483
01:11:28,973 --> 01:11:32,500
What?
What are you talking about, my Osman?

484
01:11:32,500 --> 01:11:34,836
She admitted it.

485
01:11:34,836 --> 01:11:38,836
She did it to save his captive
father from Nicola.

486
01:11:39,829 --> 01:11:45,649
What I want is to make Nicola believe
that his game is still on.

487
01:11:45,820 --> 01:11:47,850
I want to trick him, my Bala.

488
01:11:51,221 --> 01:11:53,651
That's why I marry her.

489
01:11:53,966 --> 01:11:59,546
- Is this the reason?
- Of course.

490
01:12:05,212 --> 01:12:11,392
Then I don't agree you marrying her.

491
01:12:12,905 --> 01:12:15,945
- Even if it's a part of your game...
- Can I come in?

492
01:12:17,527 --> 01:12:20,997
Come, aunt.
Don't tell anyone for now.

493
01:12:21,064 --> 01:12:23,034
Come.

494
01:12:30,614 --> 01:12:35,124
- Son.
- Speak, aunt.

495
01:12:37,871 --> 01:12:40,081
Ayaz Alp.

496
01:12:43,768 --> 01:12:46,288
He has been martyred.

497
01:12:56,626 --> 01:12:58,416
Ayaz.

498
01:13:17,923 --> 01:13:26,313
Inna Lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un.
("Verily we belong to Allah, and
verily to Him do we return.")

499
01:13:39,398 --> 01:13:42,268
I will make them pay!

500
01:13:42,315 --> 01:13:46,385
I will take revenge from whoever did this!

501
01:14:02,200 --> 01:14:06,410
The man who you are going to take
revenge from left this note on Ayaz Alp.

502
01:14:13,727 --> 01:14:16,737
Lion hunter Vladius.

503
01:14:21,159 --> 01:14:24,349
Lion hunter Vladius.

504
01:14:25,280 --> 01:14:27,180
Vladius!

505
01:14:27,684 --> 01:14:29,670
Vladius!

506
01:14:29,670 --> 01:14:34,750
You killed my brother!
Ignoble dog!

507
01:14:36,581 --> 01:14:40,291
I'll kill you!

508
01:14:42,206 --> 01:14:44,456
I'll kill you!

509
01:14:47,341 --> 01:14:50,901
Aunt, give us a minute.

510
01:15:09,732 --> 01:15:13,882
My heart is burning, brother.
Tell me what you have to say.

511
01:15:13,932 --> 01:15:16,342
My condolences, brother.

512
01:15:17,552 --> 01:15:21,502
I heard about the Kulucahisar.
May your conquer be blessed.

513
01:15:22,513 --> 01:15:27,153
What can I say, Osman?
You made Geyhatu our enemy.

514
01:15:28,992 --> 01:15:32,762
You put Kayıs in a difficult
situation.

515
01:15:33,045 --> 01:15:37,935
They will arrive here anytime.

516
01:15:39,993 --> 01:15:45,703
After that move, we seperated forever.

517
01:15:45,808 --> 01:15:50,878
Your path is selfishness.
My path is about the future of this tribe.

518
01:15:50,958 --> 01:15:54,618
Our paths have never crossed anyways,
brother.

519
01:15:55,485 --> 01:16:00,065
Don't be afraid of Geyhatu.
I'll handle it.

520
01:16:11,473 --> 01:16:13,613
Ah, Osman, ah.

521
01:16:14,250 --> 01:16:18,730
Oh my brother.
How can you handle?

522
01:16:18,742 --> 01:16:20,222
How?

523
01:16:24,470 --> 01:16:30,250
Don't worry brother.
I know what to do .

524
01:16:32,526 --> 01:16:37,456
Let me visit my martyr now.

525
01:17:17,957 --> 01:17:20,117
Brother.

526
01:17:24,689 --> 01:17:26,549
Brother.

527
01:17:37,360 --> 01:17:39,450
My Ayaz.

528
01:17:40,183 --> 01:17:42,253
My Ayaz.

529
01:17:45,006 --> 01:17:47,666
So you wanted to leave early.

530
01:17:48,439 --> 01:17:53,139
Is that right, my Ayaz?
Did you want to leave early?

531
01:17:53,676 --> 01:17:59,736
You wanted to arrive at our Lord's
heaven.

532
01:18:03,839 --> 01:18:06,449
You deserved it brother.

533
01:18:10,805 --> 01:18:12,295
You deserved it.

534
01:18:17,591 --> 01:18:19,251
Thank to Allah.

535
01:18:22,024 --> 01:18:25,134
Thank to our Lord.

536
01:18:27,075 --> 01:18:30,865
I have brothers who know the
meaning of martyr.

537
01:18:34,619 --> 01:18:41,139
And they console themselves with...

538
01:18:41,930 --> 01:18:44,920
shadada.

539
01:18:56,518 --> 01:19:02,018
A big, strong and faithul brother he was.

540
01:19:05,841 --> 01:19:09,041
Tell his story to kids of Kayı.

541
01:19:13,316 --> 01:19:15,426
My Ayaz.

542
01:19:29,670 --> 01:19:32,480
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(in the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

543
01:19:59,610 --> 01:20:03,629
Targun Hatun works for Nicola.

544
01:20:03,629 --> 01:20:06,393
She did it to save his father who
was captured by Nicola.

545
01:20:06,393 --> 01:20:11,873
What I want is that Nicola keeps
believing that his game is still on.

546
01:20:12,682 --> 01:20:15,202
I will trick them, my Bala.

547
01:20:17,160 --> 01:20:19,380
This is why I marry her.

548
01:20:37,691 --> 01:20:39,241
Bala.

549
01:20:49,891 --> 01:20:53,391
- Are you fine, my beautiful daughter?
- I'm fine mother.

550
01:20:53,932 --> 01:20:56,412
Why would I be not fine?

551
01:20:56,879 --> 01:21:00,129
You are lost in thoughts all alone.

552
01:21:02,468 --> 01:21:06,008
I was thinking about what a
great guy Osman Bey is.

553
01:21:07,306 --> 01:21:11,306
Of course, he is.
He is, but...

554
01:21:12,504 --> 01:21:14,774
Aren't you offended at all, Bala?

555
01:21:15,032 --> 01:21:17,742
For now, no one should know.

556
01:21:17,742 --> 01:21:20,912
Aren't you sad at all?

557
01:21:22,839 --> 01:21:26,509
Why should we talk about that, Gonca?

558
01:21:27,757 --> 01:21:31,117
Everything happens as it's destined.

559
01:21:31,673 --> 01:21:37,423
Today, we conquered Kulucahisar. We fought
together just like the old days.

560
01:21:38,815 --> 01:21:44,365
Right, Aygül?
How did we strike at the heathens?

561
01:21:44,576 --> 01:21:49,436
We did indeed. Now our swords are
freed from their sheathes.

562
01:21:49,436 --> 01:21:52,926
Osman Bey won't stop the holy war.

563
01:22:01,657 --> 01:22:07,977
It would be so sweet now if we hadn't
received bad news from Ayaz Alp.

564
01:22:08,233 --> 01:22:13,773
Then we'll pray for our martyr,
and make his soul proud.

565
01:22:15,192 --> 01:22:19,652
-Bring Osman's Qur-an.
-Yes, Selcan Mother.

566
01:22:38,640 --> 01:22:42,640
He said that he will take Kulucahisar
and he did.

567
01:22:42,966 --> 01:22:46,966
If he says that he'll take İnegöl
and do it...

568
01:22:48,315 --> 01:22:56,755
...who can do anything? After now,
telling him that he can't don't matter.

569
01:22:58,607 --> 01:23:05,957
Our laws allow us to select a Bey
before Ertuğrul Bey recovers.

570
01:23:06,492 --> 01:23:13,332
In this time of conflict, the election
of the Bey must be done.

571
01:23:13,545 --> 01:23:17,545
Without a Bey, Osman won't listen to
anyone.

572
01:23:18,952 --> 01:23:22,952
Are we sure that the beys in the
tents won't support Osman?

573
01:23:23,352 --> 01:23:28,772
We'll tell them about the situation and
show them the dangers we are facing.

574
01:23:30,502 --> 01:23:39,342
-Osman won't listen to this decision, uncle.
-Then we'll try every way, including exile.

575
01:23:40,681 --> 01:23:46,391
If needed, we will shed blood for
the future of the tents.

576
01:23:49,028 --> 01:23:53,328
I said if needed. If needed, my nephew.

577
01:23:59,918 --> 01:24:08,568
-What about Bamsı Bey?
-We should convince him before it gets to that.

578
01:24:09,628 --> 01:24:13,110
You'll do that.

579
01:24:21,373 --> 01:24:26,183
Tomorrow, we should start talking to
the beys.

580
01:24:26,288 --> 01:24:31,718
You are right, uncle.
We should.

581
01:24:34,045 --> 01:24:37,105
Inegöl Castle.

582
01:24:39,877 --> 01:24:44,697
Wow, wow, wow. İnal Bey.

583
01:24:48,139 --> 01:24:52,139
It's a great honor to see you here, İnal Bey.

584
01:24:53,663 --> 01:25:02,653
Now you must be thinking. ''What did I do
to sit here instead of eating with the rats.''

585
01:25:03,532 --> 01:25:09,012
For a captive, rats or mouses make
no difference.

586
01:25:09,030 --> 01:25:13,670
Whoever accompanies you, the food
is still a poison.

587
01:25:15,184 --> 01:25:20,104
These Turks never change.

588
01:25:20,123 --> 01:25:25,183
-I guess you don't like captivity.
-If you had the same blood...

589
01:25:25,183 --> 01:25:30,411
...you would kill yourself after all
those defeats.

590
01:25:31,822 --> 01:25:38,232
I already died, İnal Bey.
But I've reborn again.

591
01:25:38,232 --> 01:25:42,232
Do you know why, huh?

592
01:25:42,508 --> 01:25:48,588
To banish your kind, the Turks
from these lands.

593
01:25:48,607 --> 01:25:52,607
You'll die a lot, Nikola.

594
01:25:54,630 --> 01:25:58,630
I won't die this time.
Do you know who'll die?

595
01:26:00,648 --> 01:26:02,948
Osman.

596
01:26:03,066 --> 01:26:09,976
And who will kill Osman?
Who will? Who?

597
01:26:12,630 --> 01:26:19,590
Helen. I think we should send a word
to Targun Hatun. We should say...

598
01:26:19,590 --> 01:26:23,550
...if she doesn't kill Osman,
Lord Nikola...

599
01:26:23,550 --> 01:26:27,550
...will use your father's bones...

600
01:26:28,494 --> 01:26:32,704
...to make a necklace.
A necklace.

601
01:26:32,704 --> 01:26:36,704
You can't do this!
They will kill my daughter!

602
01:26:36,704 --> 01:26:41,814
Your daughter isn't so alive while you
are in my hands anyway, İnal Bey.

603
01:27:00,965 --> 01:27:04,965
-Take him away.
-Let me go.

604
01:27:05,292 --> 01:27:09,292
As he deserves.
A room with the rats.

605
01:27:20,881 --> 01:27:29,811
Helen. While Targun Hatun kills Osman,
you'll kill Bamsı Bey who defends him.

606
01:27:31,145 --> 01:27:36,035
You are sending me to death, Nikola?

607
01:27:37,841 --> 01:27:43,091
Don't go to death, Helen.
Send Bamsı instead.

608
01:27:45,478 --> 01:27:48,598
I don't like excuses.

609
01:28:39,376 --> 01:28:41,916
Thank you, wife.

610
01:28:52,616 --> 01:29:01,376
What are you thinking? It's been
a while since I saw that expression.

611
01:29:03,031 --> 01:29:06,161
What expression?

612
01:29:07,824 --> 01:29:13,994
The expression of 'I know what to
do to you'.

613
01:29:20,378 --> 01:29:25,348
Tomorrow, I'll talk to the beys.

614
01:29:26,099 --> 01:29:34,929
Before my brother dies, the next bey
should be elected.

615
01:29:36,497 --> 01:29:40,497
Before your brother dies?

616
01:29:41,405 --> 01:29:49,515
Yes. While Osman struggles with Nikola,
we'll gather the council.

617
01:29:51,441 --> 01:29:57,671
Savcı will seek it and it's possible that
he'll win.

618
01:29:59,053 --> 01:30:04,922
-So?
-So, Osman won't have it.

619
01:30:04,922 --> 01:30:10,952
-They'll draw swords...
-Then?

620
01:30:11,096 --> 01:30:16,236
One dies, the other becomes a
brother-slayer.

621
01:30:16,921 --> 01:30:23,411
-Only Gündüz and I will be left.
-Then? Then?

622
01:30:23,681 --> 01:30:27,681
Then, it's apparent.

623
01:30:30,264 --> 01:30:34,264
I'll be the Bey of the Kayı.

624
01:30:38,276 --> 01:30:43,656
Finally. Finally!

625
01:30:45,230 --> 01:30:51,510
Finally, Dündar Bey!
Be like that all the time.

626
01:30:51,519 --> 01:30:57,059
Be like that so that I can support
you with all my heart and power.

627
01:30:59,677 --> 01:31:06,267
Now, you gave me
a real purpose.

628
01:31:09,478 --> 01:31:15,638
You woke me up from dead sleep.

629
01:31:32,017 --> 01:31:37,157
My brother Osman wants the
best for the Kayı.

630
01:31:37,663 --> 01:31:42,733
He thinks that the best is the destruction
of all enemies.

631
01:31:44,204 --> 01:31:47,564
He struggles for that.

632
01:31:48,986 --> 01:31:53,946
Allah knows that he is doing well.

633
01:31:56,286 --> 01:31:59,696
He saved me from captivity twice.

634
01:32:00,450 --> 01:32:06,600
He reconquered Kulucahisar.
He saved Söğüt.

635
01:32:08,783 --> 01:32:11,993
We are in his debt.

636
01:32:24,675 --> 01:32:29,995
What are you saying, Savcı?

637
01:32:30,881 --> 01:32:42,991
But he doesn't know that the enemy
grows and the Kayı can't get on with that.

638
01:32:44,015 --> 01:32:49,165
For the future of the Kayı,
he must be stopped.

639
01:32:53,969 --> 01:32:56,759
How will that happen?

640
01:32:59,038 --> 01:33:05,378
For this to be taken care of lawfully,
the council should gather before...

641
01:33:05,387 --> 01:33:09,177
...my father Ertuğrul Ghazi passes away.
And I should be elected.

642
01:33:11,977 --> 01:33:14,337
Gündüz?

643
01:33:14,987 --> 01:33:19,557
I'm not sure about him.
He is too fond of my brother Osman.

644
01:33:22,975 --> 01:33:25,815
What about Dündar Bey.

645
01:33:28,494 --> 01:33:31,634
He will support me.

646
01:33:33,652 --> 01:33:36,502
He is the one that you shouldn't
be sure about.

647
01:33:39,437 --> 01:33:43,977
What do you mean, wife?
Have you heard something.

648
01:33:45,399 --> 01:33:49,959
Even if Dündar Bey wants to give up,
Hazal Hatun won't.

649
01:33:50,265 --> 01:33:59,559
We might be on the same side because of
Osman. But without him, we'll be enemies.

650
01:34:00,249 --> 01:34:02,909
You should know that.

651
01:34:33,433 --> 01:34:41,953
My Allah, Kulucahisar Castle is
reconquered with your bless.

652
01:34:43,421 --> 01:34:47,421
And it is a property of Islam, again.

653
01:34:47,794 --> 01:35:00,934
O' Allah, without your bless, we wouldn't
be honored with Islam, or the holy war.

654
01:35:02,023 --> 01:35:09,603
We bow our heads to your blessing.

655
01:35:11,084 --> 01:35:17,514
Don't make us think that it is us
who wins the victory.

656
01:35:18,343 --> 01:35:26,593
Protect us from conceit, arrogance, greed.

657
01:35:28,301 --> 01:35:34,661
O' Allah, don't let us be like
the heathen.

658
01:35:34,961 --> 01:35:43,331
Make our brother Azad a neighbor
to the companions of our prophet...

659
01:35:43,331 --> 01:35:50,811
...for being a martyr in the holy war.

660
01:35:50,811 --> 01:35:56,571
-Amin.
-O' Allah, these Ghazis who opened their hands...

661
01:35:56,571 --> 01:36:03,231
...ask for the same fate.
-Amin.

662
01:36:26,748 --> 01:36:29,448
Hear our prayers, my Allah.

663
01:36:50,632 --> 01:36:55,912
Tomorrow is the day of holy war.

664
01:36:55,912 --> 01:37:02,190
You'll come with me.
And the alps that are left here...

665
01:37:02,190 --> 01:37:09,060
...will do their last duty for our
martyr brother.

666
01:37:09,207 --> 01:37:13,207
-As you command, my bey.
-As you command, my bey.

667
01:37:15,962 --> 01:37:19,713
Gence Bey, come with us tomorrow.

668
01:37:19,713 --> 01:37:24,003
-My path is your path, Osman Bey.
-Thank you.

669
01:37:26,773 --> 01:37:31,723
Yavlak Arslan's men don't know you.
You should scout the way.

670
01:37:32,217 --> 01:37:36,217
And tell us if there is a trap.

671
01:37:36,217 --> 01:37:40,897
Will I draw my sword and join
the holy war then, Osman Bey?

672
01:37:41,131 --> 01:37:45,131
That's up to you.

673
01:37:58,483 --> 01:38:02,483
Come, come. Bring it, my girl.
Bring it.

674
01:38:04,747 --> 01:38:08,747
Just like that, show it to
Targun Hatun.

675
01:38:16,767 --> 01:38:22,233
Targun, you'll be the wife of
a Kayı bey.

676
01:38:22,233 --> 01:38:27,173
Your aunt Hazal will have a pretty
dress sewed for you.

677
01:38:27,846 --> 01:38:33,966
You can take off your steppe clothing
and wear those in the tents.

678
01:38:33,966 --> 01:38:39,556
Thank you but I'm not used to
wearing such fancy things.

679
01:38:39,556 --> 01:38:46,356
No way. You are a new bride.
You should be fancy.

680
01:38:47,190 --> 01:38:49,940
Thank you.

681
01:38:59,342 --> 01:39:02,132
It's very pretty.

682
01:39:05,650 --> 01:39:11,600
Selcan Hatun, are you empty-handed?

683
01:39:12,914 --> 01:39:18,294
Giving a gift to the new bride
is of our customs.

684
01:39:20,913 --> 01:39:23,953
Have you forgotten it?

685
01:39:24,069 --> 01:39:29,519
The best gift is an advice, my girl.
That's all I can give you.

686
01:39:34,967 --> 01:39:40,477
Is stinginess called advice now,
Selcan Hatun?

687
01:39:44,089 --> 01:39:50,519
Look, my girl, a fire can burn down
the tents.

688
01:39:50,519 --> 01:39:56,109
And fire can cook food.

689
01:40:05,446 --> 01:40:12,006
Your fire should bring light to your
husband and the tents.

690
01:40:15,088 --> 01:40:20,968
Be like a drop of water.
But don't forget...

691
01:40:21,047 --> 01:40:26,417
...a drop of water stinks when it touches
hot iron, and becomes a poison in a viper's mouth.

692
01:40:49,582 --> 01:40:54,592
Be the mother of pearl so that it can
be a pearl in your mouth.

693
01:40:57,876 --> 01:41:05,616
Be like soil, my girl. But don't forget.
Both thorn and herb grow on soil.

694
01:41:13,069 --> 01:41:17,769
For this reason, be like a flower,
my girl.

695
01:41:28,645 --> 01:41:30,815
Enjoy your meal.

696
01:42:00,156 --> 01:42:07,346
What a great honor, Geyhatu!
You gave me a seat after my request.

697
01:42:09,371 --> 01:42:13,961
You wanted a place to sit.
I told you to go...

698
01:42:14,597 --> 01:42:22,347
...and sit at Kulucahisar.
Osman took that castle from you.

699
01:42:24,689 --> 01:42:31,539
Now, you need a seat
to sit. Sit.

700
01:42:32,653 --> 01:42:36,303
Not sitting was better, it seems.

701
01:42:36,303 --> 01:42:40,303
Stop grumbling. Sit.

702
01:42:57,043 --> 01:43:03,133
-Speak.
-Osman stepped over your order, Geyhatu.

703
01:43:03,363 --> 01:43:09,903
While I was expecting peace in
Yavlak Arslan's tent, he took Kulucahisar.

704
01:43:09,903 --> 01:43:15,903
The castle that you gave me.
So, Osman took your castle.

705
01:43:16,066 --> 01:43:20,066
Can't Yavlak Arslan control Osman?

706
01:43:21,199 --> 01:43:25,199
No, only you can control
Osman?

707
01:43:29,502 --> 01:43:35,402
What if I kill all of you and
give everything to Osman...

708
01:43:35,402 --> 01:43:39,402
...make him the Bey of Beys?

709
01:43:40,721 --> 01:43:44,891
Tell me why this
would be wrong.

710
01:43:44,891 --> 01:43:48,891
Speak. I want to know you.

711
01:43:50,581 --> 01:43:55,741
I'll be honored. You made
Yavlak Arslan your margrave.

712
01:43:56,145 --> 01:44:01,705
But his real purpose is to destroy you
and build a Turkish state in Anatolia.

713
01:44:02,138 --> 01:44:06,138
But don't be afraid.
He can't do such a thing.

714
01:44:06,138 --> 01:44:11,578
If you ask what I want,
I want to banish all the Turks.

715
01:44:12,084 --> 01:44:16,084
Mongols can stay.

716
01:44:18,630 --> 01:44:23,230
-Why?
-Because you aren't Muslim.

717
01:44:23,522 --> 01:44:29,922
Neither Rome nor I have a problem
with you.

718
01:44:30,471 --> 01:44:34,730
What about Osman?

719
01:44:34,730 --> 01:44:39,720
If you make Osman the Bey of Beys,
and if he gets the pledge of all Turks...

720
01:44:40,200 --> 01:44:45,780
...then, Geyhatu, neither Rome
nor the Mongols can stand.

721
01:44:46,786 --> 01:44:50,786
Osman scared you.

722
01:44:56,392 --> 01:45:03,852
Osman should scare you, too, Geyhatu.
It should so that you can solve the problem.

723
01:45:04,404 --> 01:45:07,794
I like advices.

724
01:45:10,429 --> 01:45:13,679
Tie him in where he sits.

725
01:45:14,263 --> 01:45:18,263
What is this now?
What is this?

726
01:45:19,912 --> 01:45:26,102
What kind of diplomacy is this?
Is this steppe diplomacy.

727
01:45:41,467 --> 01:45:45,467
-Take him away.
-Barbarian.

728
01:45:45,467 --> 01:45:48,777
This is how you should sit
at İnegöl.

729
01:45:48,777 --> 01:45:51,177
So that Osman can't take your seat.

730
01:45:58,388 --> 01:46:01,448
Little lord is gone.

731
01:46:02,284 --> 01:46:08,874
What should we do with that Osman?
Möngke? Möngke?

732
01:46:09,127 --> 01:46:12,877
Should we behead Osman?

733
01:46:12,877 --> 01:46:19,247
Or should we boil him
with his brothers?

734
01:46:19,393 --> 01:46:22,263
Mongke? Möngke?

735
01:46:26,605 --> 01:46:30,605
Möngke isn't here.
Möngke is dead.

736
01:46:32,014 --> 01:46:34,384
Möngke is dead.

737
01:47:11,251 --> 01:47:14,591
Osman Bey! Osman Bey!
Osman Bey!

738
01:47:18,999 --> 01:47:21,269
Osman Bey!

739
01:47:22,935 --> 01:47:26,385
You are making a great mistake,
Osman Bey.

740
01:47:26,557 --> 01:47:31,527
-What is that mistake?
-Yavlak Arslan.

741
01:47:34,653 --> 01:47:39,783
You shouldn't incur Yavlak Arslan.
It will be a shame.

742
01:47:43,091 --> 01:47:47,091
You deserve a better death.

743
01:47:50,704 --> 01:47:55,344
Our lives are in the hands
of Allah.

744
01:47:58,113 --> 01:48:02,903
We'll die as he wants.

745
01:48:12,271 --> 01:48:14,121
I wish to die standing.

746
01:48:30,148 --> 01:48:33,658
Thank you, Cerkutay.
Thank you.

747
01:48:34,900 --> 01:48:37,780
If I have to kill you, I'll
remember what you've just said.

748
01:48:41,976 --> 01:48:44,186
You grovel...

749
01:48:45,123 --> 01:48:47,053
I'll kill you standing.

750
01:49:18,993 --> 01:49:23,473
- You're not a Muslim, right?
- Yes.

751
01:49:24,052 --> 01:49:26,945
Will you be a Muslim
when you marry Osman Bey?

752
01:49:26,945 --> 01:49:30,658
She'll become a
Muslim first, then she'll marry him.

753
01:49:30,658 --> 01:49:31,788
Yes.

754
01:49:44,861 --> 01:49:47,431
Excuse me, Hatuns.

755
01:49:51,915 --> 01:49:54,895
Let's see what you're up to.

756
01:50:01,104 --> 01:50:02,714
Oh.

757
01:50:34,969 --> 01:50:36,909
Sit, daughter.

758
01:50:44,632 --> 01:50:46,222
My Bala.

759
01:50:46,641 --> 01:50:48,481
My beautiful daughter.

760
01:50:49,639 --> 01:50:51,059
My darling.

761
01:50:52,856 --> 01:50:54,686
Well done.

762
01:50:55,019 --> 01:50:59,719
You showed everyone how Sheikh Edebalı's
daughter should be.

763
01:51:00,589 --> 01:51:04,169
Always be like that.

764
01:51:06,429 --> 01:51:10,429
Why don't you say yourself?
I've learned so much from you.

765
01:51:12,545 --> 01:51:14,785
Yes you have.

766
01:51:15,357 --> 01:51:19,357
However, you have.

767
01:51:19,567 --> 01:51:21,087
Look at Hazal.

768
01:51:21,676 --> 01:51:24,946
I've done many things but...

769
01:51:25,106 --> 01:51:28,896
Hazal is still the same.

770
01:51:32,156 --> 01:51:34,526
- Bala!
- What happened?

771
01:51:34,699 --> 01:51:38,879
Targun Hatun left the tent.
Aygül followed her.

772
01:51:40,361 --> 01:51:43,561
Go follow her..

773
01:51:43,721 --> 01:51:45,861
Look after her.

774
01:51:45,964 --> 01:51:49,964
Let's not disappoint Osman.

775
01:52:01,199 --> 01:52:04,999
My Bey, there are
Yavlak Arslan's guards ahead.

776
01:52:05,712 --> 01:52:07,872
Thanks, brother.

777
01:52:10,435 --> 01:52:12,925
Yavlak Arslan set a trap.

778
01:52:16,976 --> 01:52:19,516
I know what to do.

779
01:52:45,170 --> 01:52:48,150
They're coming.

780
01:52:48,986 --> 01:52:50,706
Come, Osman.

781
01:52:52,183 --> 01:52:55,783
Get ready. Wait until they come.

782
01:52:56,367 --> 01:53:00,137
If they fight, they will fight
in a wounded body.

783
01:53:16,766 --> 01:53:19,416
Get ready. Wait for my sign.

784
01:53:21,178 --> 01:53:22,958
Wait.

785
01:53:25,507 --> 01:53:27,027
Wait.

786
01:53:28,565 --> 01:53:30,565
Wait.

787
01:54:14,093 --> 01:54:17,393
- They are our watchmen.
- Damn it!

788
01:54:56,328 --> 01:54:57,928
Yavlak Arslan!

789
01:55:02,080 --> 01:55:04,920
Now we'll talk in your way of
understanding.

790
01:55:46,676 --> 01:55:51,586
Brothers, tie them to our horses.

791
01:55:57,777 --> 01:56:00,047
- Come on!
- Make them wear your clothes.

792
01:56:34,333 --> 01:56:38,233
You'll give an account for
your traps, your treasons...

793
01:56:38,554 --> 01:56:41,424
and your harms.

794
01:57:10,602 --> 01:57:11,862
My Bey.

795
01:57:12,147 --> 01:57:14,917
This endless war harms us.

796
01:57:15,016 --> 01:57:18,796
No one asks how people is.

797
01:57:18,825 --> 01:57:21,055
Söğüt is also the same.

798
01:57:21,065 --> 01:57:25,585
The people can't do anything for
fear of Nikola's attack.

799
01:57:26,498 --> 01:57:28,708
We need peace.

800
01:57:28,937 --> 01:57:29,887
However...

801
01:57:32,324 --> 01:57:35,004
it's not possible because of Osman Bey.

802
01:57:40,445 --> 01:57:43,635
Now we're in trouble because of Geyhatu.

803
01:57:43,642 --> 01:57:49,942
We'll die starving if we can't sell goods.

804
01:57:53,835 --> 01:57:56,195
Do you want a solution from us?

805
01:57:56,980 --> 01:58:00,420
If you can't find a solution, how
can we find any?

806
01:58:04,490 --> 01:58:07,460
Consult our Bey, Ertuğrul Ghazi.

807
01:58:14,580 --> 01:58:19,030
We wouldn't be like
that if Ertuğrul Bey was healthy.

808
01:58:21,491 --> 01:58:24,971
Anyone who holds a seal is the ruler.

809
01:58:28,153 --> 01:58:31,833
When he has the seal, what can we do?

810
01:58:35,063 --> 01:58:38,523
Savcı Bey is right.

811
01:58:39,507 --> 01:58:44,537
We need to elect a new Bey...

812
01:58:45,188 --> 01:58:48,638
to make things better and
prevent Osman from preventing it.

813
01:58:52,400 --> 01:58:55,840
May Allah make it late.

814
01:58:55,898 --> 01:58:59,118
It'll be a mistake to do that before my
father dies.

815
01:59:00,362 --> 01:59:03,962
Osman will refuse that.

816
01:59:04,802 --> 01:59:07,602
It's the right thing to do.

817
01:59:08,721 --> 01:59:11,251
Choose your side, Gündüz Bey.

818
01:59:11,373 --> 01:59:13,733
You're the only one left.

819
01:59:15,290 --> 01:59:17,140
You still don't understand, do you?

820
01:59:18,728 --> 01:59:20,928
Then let me say.

821
01:59:22,236 --> 01:59:25,106
I side with Ertuğrul Ghazi.

822
01:59:27,285 --> 01:59:31,655
I don't want to hear about Beys
as long as he is alive.

823
01:59:35,392 --> 01:59:37,242
Savcı...

824
01:59:39,141 --> 01:59:43,141
you still fight with Osman.

825
01:59:47,681 --> 01:59:49,241
However, you should know that.

826
01:59:50,681 --> 01:59:52,941
I won't be like you.

827
01:59:55,687 --> 01:59:57,807
I'm with my father.

828
02:00:05,431 --> 02:00:09,431
When the time comes... I'll be
with...

829
02:00:12,281 --> 02:00:14,591
whoever he wants.

830
02:00:18,554 --> 02:00:20,504
If you excuse me, uncle.

831
02:00:28,348 --> 02:00:29,428
At least...

832
02:00:31,101 --> 02:00:32,391
He chose his side.

833
02:00:33,974 --> 02:00:37,024
Choose your sides, brothers.

834
02:00:37,601 --> 02:00:41,051
Do you want an infinite war or...

835
02:00:42,051 --> 02:00:47,221
a tent which grows and gets
rich day by day?

836
02:01:03,747 --> 02:01:07,427
Osman Bey and Bamsı Bey
won't forgive that.

837
02:01:09,129 --> 02:01:11,379
I'll talk to Bamsı Bey.

838
02:01:12,277 --> 02:01:14,807
He loves me, he'll listen.

839
02:01:16,106 --> 02:01:17,846
He has to.

840
02:01:25,588 --> 02:01:30,748
You can't kill me, Osman. You're
not that dumb.

841
02:01:32,609 --> 02:01:36,029
If you kill me, all the Turk Beys...

842
02:01:36,390 --> 02:01:40,390
will become your enemy, not just Beyhatu.

843
02:01:40,926 --> 02:01:43,856
Don't worry.

844
02:01:45,398 --> 02:01:48,018
Think about what you'll say.

845
02:01:50,708 --> 02:01:52,568
Tie them all.

846
02:02:19,449 --> 02:02:21,079
Kumral Abdal.

847
02:02:24,914 --> 02:02:26,144
Osman Bey.

848
02:02:28,090 --> 02:02:31,750
Look at this boy. I have
hope from him.

849
02:02:37,559 --> 02:02:40,399
Easy, Kumral Abdal.

850
02:02:40,479 --> 02:02:44,749
Don't worry. The rest is ours.

851
02:02:53,320 --> 02:02:56,480
Your mystery is solved.

852
02:03:17,819 --> 02:03:20,009
Bungler.

853
02:03:38,899 --> 02:03:44,289
- What is Yavlak Arslan doing there?
- So, Möngke and Cerkutay's partner...

854
02:03:45,120 --> 02:03:47,040
is Yavlak.

855
02:03:47,791 --> 02:03:50,251
He got into deep water.

856
02:03:50,351 --> 02:03:52,361
What will we do now?

857
02:03:52,865 --> 02:03:55,395
Yavlak will win.

858
02:03:55,564 --> 02:03:57,914
Osman will lose.

859
02:03:58,354 --> 02:04:03,274
Geyhatu and Çobanoğulları will fight.

860
02:04:06,538 --> 02:04:08,818
Let's save Yavlak.

861
02:04:09,195 --> 02:04:11,725
Then let's kill Osman.

862
02:04:52,802 --> 02:04:54,742
I knew you were a traitor.

863
02:04:58,315 --> 02:04:59,905
Targun!

864
02:05:07,820 --> 02:05:09,950
Come here!

865
02:05:16,088 --> 02:05:18,278
I saw you swallowed the paper.

866
02:05:18,991 --> 02:05:21,341
You can't run away.

867
02:05:22,641 --> 02:05:24,521
Traitor dog!

868
02:05:24,931 --> 02:05:27,821
You lied to Osman Bey.

869
02:05:28,482 --> 02:05:31,654
It's none of your business...

870
02:05:31,654 --> 02:05:33,454
Osman Bey has a beautiful hatun.

871
02:06:00,627 --> 02:06:03,067
You always saw me as an enemy.

872
02:06:03,819 --> 02:06:06,749
However, just our paths were different.

873
02:06:08,488 --> 02:06:11,478
I was going to kill Geyhatu.

874
02:06:12,461 --> 02:06:18,291
So, I was going to end the
Mongol oppression.

875
02:06:22,921 --> 02:06:25,901
I underestimated you.

876
02:06:26,696 --> 02:06:29,436
So that you were going to
end the oppression...

877
02:06:29,915 --> 02:06:31,704
What were you doing with Möngke?

878
02:06:31,884 --> 02:06:35,884
Möngke is an idiot.

879
02:06:36,658 --> 02:06:40,658
Osman, it's still not too late...

880
02:06:41,156 --> 02:06:43,126
for a powerful Turk
state in Anatolia.

881
02:06:43,157 --> 02:06:44,477
What are you saying?

882
02:06:44,608 --> 02:06:47,298
Geyhatu should die today.

883
02:06:49,961 --> 02:06:52,901
Or it'll be too late for all of us.

884
02:07:04,124 --> 02:07:05,974
My Bey!

885
02:07:12,035 --> 02:07:13,255
My Bey!

886
02:07:22,762 --> 02:07:24,662
My Bey!

887
02:07:25,110 --> 02:07:27,440
Are you fine, my Bey?

888
02:07:33,329 --> 02:07:34,809
Flatyos.

889
02:08:06,440 --> 02:08:07,790
What, Osman?

890
02:08:08,958 --> 02:08:11,498
Can't you hold a sword?

891
02:08:13,614 --> 02:08:15,144
Don't worry.

892
02:08:15,812 --> 02:08:17,912
I'll take care of you.

893
02:08:33,450 --> 02:08:35,980
Don't forget that I've saved you, Yavlak.

894
02:08:37,831 --> 02:08:39,501
Let's kill Osman now.

895
02:08:39,618 --> 02:08:42,898
You know, when you hurt a lion...

896
02:08:44,315 --> 02:08:46,655
you should kill it.

897
02:08:48,599 --> 02:08:53,489
I'm grateful to you and Nikola.

898
02:09:37,691 --> 02:09:39,911
What are you up to again, Targun?

899
02:09:40,425 --> 02:09:41,885
Put your sword down.

900
02:09:42,127 --> 02:09:46,127
- I didn't do anything wrong.
- Osman Bey told us some things.

901
02:09:48,512 --> 02:09:51,292
However, I see there's something else.

902
02:10:01,561 --> 02:10:02,631
Targun!

903
02:10:03,057 --> 02:10:07,997
Do you want to save your father or
cause trouble?

904
02:10:15,080 --> 02:10:17,080
- Traitor!
- Stop, Aygül.

905
02:10:17,490 --> 02:10:19,400
Who was he?

906
02:10:21,645 --> 02:10:24,225
What was written on that paper?

907
02:10:27,555 --> 02:10:28,995
What paper?

908
02:10:33,256 --> 02:10:36,616
If everyone knows, it's
not a secret, Bala.

909
02:10:40,022 --> 02:10:42,542
What secret is she talking about?

910
02:10:46,004 --> 02:10:49,654
Whatever. Let's talk in the tent.

911
02:10:51,993 --> 02:10:53,313
Come on.

912
02:10:54,007 --> 02:10:55,627
Come on!

913
02:11:09,400 --> 02:11:13,910
I said you'll see Azrael.

914
02:11:22,454 --> 02:11:25,134
No one can take our lives...

915
02:11:26,637 --> 02:11:29,047
that Allah gives..

916
02:11:30,089 --> 02:11:32,809
to us.

917
02:11:33,783 --> 02:11:46,503
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com